+.TH BAKE 1
+.SH NAME
+bake \- bootstrappable recipe runner
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+.B bake
+.RB [ --file " FILE"]
+.RI [ TARGET ]
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+Runs a target after its dependencies, once per invocation. The default input
+is build.bake and the default target is its first named target.
+Commands are executed directly, not through a shell. A failed command aborts
+the build. Dependency cycles and unknown requested targets are errors.
+.SH RECIPE SYNTAX
+.TP
+.B : target dependencies
+Defines a target and its prerequisite targets. Following command lines belong
+to this target. Prerequisites with no recipe are treated as source inputs.
+.TP
+.B : first second :
+Shares a command list between named targets.
+.TP
+.B : %.out %.in
+Defines a pattern recipe for prerequisites requested by another target.
+.TP
+.B = NAME value
+Defines a variable, also available to child processes.
+.TP
+.B ${NAME}, $@, $<
+Expand an environment variable, the active target, and its first dependency.
+.TP
+.B ? NAME value command
+Runs a command when a variable matches the value. The ! form runs it when
+it does not match. Values are compared as complete strings.
+.TP
+.B cd directory
+Changes the working directory of subsequent commands.
+.TP
+.B export NAME value
+Updates the environment for subsequent commands and child processes.
+.SH NOTES
+Commands and expanded variables are split on whitespace. Quote characters
+are passed literally, not interpreted as shell quoting. An empty expansion
+is passed as an empty argument. Shell operators such as redirection and
+pipelines are not interpreted. Invoke a shell script explicitly only when
+a shell is available later in the bootstrap.
+.SH SEE ALSO
+M1(1), hex2(1), blood-elf(1)
